# Auto commit and push

When a coding task is finished (not a question-only turn), commit the relevant files and push to `origin`. Do not wait to be asked again.

- Use Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Push `HEAD` to `origin` only. Never push `upstream` (CuteLeaf/Firefly). Never force-push.
- Do not commit `素材/`, secrets, `.env*`, or unrelated files.
- If there is nothing to commit, skip. If push fails, report the error.
